# AWS Infrastructure Monitoring: CloudWatch Alarm & SNS Integration

This repository contains [Terraform](https://www.terraform.io/) configurations to set up automated monitoring and alerting for [AWS](https://aws.amazon.com/) EC2 instances. It establishes an [Amazon SNS](https://aws.amazon.com/sns/) topic coupled with an [Amazon CloudWatch](https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/) metric alarm to detect high CPU utilization.

## Architecture Overview

+------------------------+              +---------------------------+
|   EC2 Instance CPU     |  Triggers    |   Amazon CloudWatch Alarm |
|     Utilization > 80%  | -----------> |   (nautilus-cpu-alarm)    |
+------------------------+              +-------------+-------------+
|
Notifies|
v
+-------------+-------------+
|     Amazon SNS Topic      |
|    (nautilus-sns-topic)   |
+---------------------------+


## Resources Provisioned

1. **`aws_sns_topic.nautilus_sns_topic`**: 
   - A standard SNS topic named `nautilus-sns-topic` designed to receive and distribute CloudWatch alarm alerts.
2. **`aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.nautilus_cpu_alarm`**:
   - **Metric Name**: `CPUUtilization`
   - **Namespace**: `AWS/EC2`
   - **Statistic**: `Average`
   - **Period**: `300` seconds (5 minutes)
   - **Evaluation Periods**: `1`
   - **Threshold**: `80` (GreaterThanThreshold)
   - **Actions Enabled**: `true`
   - **Alarm Actions**: Linked to the ARN of `nautilus-sns-topic`.

## Outputs

The configuration exposes the following outputs for dependency mapping:
* `KKE_sns_topic_name`: The name of the SNS topic (`nautilus-sns-topic`).
* `KKE_cloudwatch_alarm_name`: The name of the CloudWatch alarm (`nautilus-cpu-alarm`).

